    "correctOptionIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Oxygen transported to all parts of the body during blood circulation is used to release energy from food.&nbsp;When the red blood cells reach tissues that need oxygen, the oxygen is released from the haemoglobin and diffuses into the cells where it is used to make energy. All the systems in our body rely on oxygen to make energy.",
