    "correctOptionIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Scientists can roughly date fossils using radiometric dating, a process that measures the&nbsp;<strong>radioactive decay of certain elements</strong>. Fossils document the existence of now-extinct species, showing that different organisms have lived on Earth during different periods of the planet's history.",
