    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "A pentadactyl forelimb in vertebrates, meaning a forelimb with five digits, serves a variety of functions depending on the animal's environment, showcasing how a single basic structure can be adapted through evolution to suit different needs, like&nbsp;swimming, flying, running, or grasping, all while maintaining the underlying five-digit pattern as a result of shared ancestry.&nbsp;",
