    "explanation": "The bacteria in the colon produce large amounts of <strong>vitamins B and K</strong> through <strong>fermentation.</strong>&nbsp;Vitamin K is a fat-soluble vitamin that helps blood clot and prevents excessive bleeding. Bacteria in the large intestine synthesize vitamins, not minerals, neither do they synthesize glucose but they do play a role in other processes that are important for the body.",
