    "text": "<p>If sales is D 12,000 and the gross profit mark -up percentage is 25%. What is the cost of sales?</p>",
    "options": [
      "D 2,400",
      "D 9,000",
      "D 9,600",
      "D 3,000"
    ],
    "correctOptionIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Calculate the gross profit using the gross profit mark-up percentage:<br>\nGross Profit = Sales Amount * (Gross Profit Mark-up Percentage / 100)<br>\nGross Profit = D12,000 * (25 / 100)<br>\nGross Profit = D12,000 * 0.25<br>\nGross Profit = D3,000<br>\n<br>\nCalculate the cost of sales by subtracting the gross profit from the sales amount:<br>\nCost of Sales = Sales Amount - Gross Profit<br>\nCost of Sales = D12,000 - D3,000<br>\nCost of Sales = D9,000<br>\n<br>\nTherefore, the cost of sales is D9,000.",
    "subject": "Accounts",
    "examType": "WAEC",
    "year": "2023"
